# The one XXL window scripts/automation/xl-run.sh xxl runs at the next Saturday
# 02:00 slot. Lives in docs/testing/ (moved 2026-09-13 so the daily review, whose write scope excludes scripts/automation/, can act as clerk). Same contract as xl-queue.env: set by the weekly review, the
# daily review acting as XL clerk (daily-review.md step 6b, from
# docs/testing/xl-pending.md), or the operator; cleared by the launcher after
# the run, so a window runs once and is never silently repeated.
#
#   XL_CHUNK   - chunk id, used for the harness log name and the ledger row
#   XL_COMMAND - the command exactly as it would be typed after
#                scripts/testing/run_and_log.sh <chunk>
#
# Empty is the normal state and the Saturday entry then exits in a second.
#
# This tier is 8 h and 754 GiB against fem-em-solver-xxl, one run per trailing
# 7 days. It is for what a 2 h xl window cannot hold -- the human-scale coil,
# or a many-drive sweep before the factorisation is reused. Ceilings are
# enforced by scripts/automation/hooks/bash_guard.py, so a command carrying a
# timeout above 28800 s or more than 16 ranks is refused before it starts.
#
# QUEUED 2026-09-13 (operator directive, interactive session) for Saturday
# 2026-09-19 02:00: WF-7 step 0b — the F-human rung at degree 2, one drive at
# 64 MHz, with the degree-1 control re-run first in the same window at the
# same rank count. Pre-registration: docs/testing/xl-pending.md entry 1.

XL_CHUNK="WF-7-step0b"
XL_COMMAND="docker compose --profile xxl exec -T fem-em-solver-xxl bash -lc 'cd /workspace && source /usr/local/bin/dolfinx-complex-mode && mkdir -p /workspace/logs && R=/workspace/logs/wf7-step0b-raw.log && { echo [orphans-before]; pgrep -c python3; true; } > \$R 2>&1; PYTHONPATH=/workspace/src FEM_EM_REQUIRE_COMPLEX=1 FEM_EM_SOLVER_PROGRESS=2 FEM_EM_WF7_DEGREE=1 timeout -k 60 1500 mpiexec -n 16 python3 scripts/probes/wf7_step0_f_human_cost.py >> \$R 2>&1; rc1=\$?; echo \"[WF-7 step0b] control degree-1 rc=\$rc1\" >> \$R; PYTHONPATH=/workspace/src FEM_EM_REQUIRE_COMPLEX=1 FEM_EM_SOLVER_PROGRESS=2 FEM_EM_WF7_DEGREE=2 timeout -k 60 27000 mpiexec -n 16 python3 scripts/probes/wf7_step0_f_human_cost.py >> \$R 2>&1; rc2=\$?; echo \"[WF-7 step0b] degree-2 rc=\$rc2\" >> \$R; { echo [orphans-after]; pgrep -c python3; true; } >> \$R 2>&1; echo \"[XL] memory.peak bytes:\" >> \$R; cat /sys/fs/cgroup/memory.peak >> \$R; rc=\$(( rc1 != 0 || rc2 != 0 )); echo \"[capture] rc=\$rc\" >> \$R; cat \$R; exit \$rc'"
